3 vector DBs:
Milvus: heavy performance
Weaviate: vector search + keyword search
Pinecone: 0 Ops


indexing: grouping vectors in the DB for narrowing down search range
one example of indexing is HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small World) algorithm, for searching vectors, every step find the 'nearest' vector, 
nearest may not be physically nearest, not necessarily the highest similarity either, it goes for the ANN (Approximate Nearest Neighbor) vector.
HNSW keeps a candidate set and explores multiple promising nodes, especially during the final search.
New vector
    ↓
Calculate its distance/similarity to existing vectors    //use Cosine similarity / Euclidean distance / Dot product AND HNSW itself
    ↓
Find suitable neighboring vectors    //greedy search, a parameter M decides maximum connections can be built at this step
    ↓
Create edges between them
    ↓
Add the new vector to the HNSW graph
